          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How steep is 40% incline in degrees?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              About 21.8 degrees. Treadmill incline is quoted as a percentage grade, rise over run, which is always a larger number than the angle: 15% is about 8.5 degrees, 30% about 16.7 degrees and 45% about 24.2 degrees.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do incline trainers need a special electrical circuit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Some do. TRUE specifies a dedicated 120-volt, 20-amp circuit for the Alpine Runner, and commercial machines commonly require one. Check the manual for the exact model before delivery, plug the machine directly into a grounded wall outlet, and have an electrician install a dedicated circuit if the maker requires it.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

